  "report": "# L001-v2 revocation under crash: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n- mutation check: 24 of 24 killed\n\nLimitations: power loss is a fsync-honest crash-image model: bytes synced before the crash are intact and nothing else is promised; it is not a real power cut (no dm-flakey, no pulled plug), it does not model a disk that lies about a flush other than as the control, a torn sector below the synced length, or the behaviour of another filesystem than the one recorded in environment.filesystem; RaftEngineLedger has no hash chain and no protected anchor, so after a lie that drops acknowledged bytes it opens without error on fewer records; undetected_rollback and engine_lie_stale_accepts count that and are descriptive, no rule reads them, and no product work is attempted on it (owner decision of 2026-10-09); the durability probe sees file data pages only; a missing directory fsync (the rename of the anchor, the creation of the log) is outside what it detects, and the model takes the directory fsync on trust; the Raft members return all their messages from one call, so the order of persisting and sending inside RaftNode::drain is not exercised; Raft runs in process on a deterministic router with no sockets and no timers, so a real network, a wall-clock election and the wire are L002's, not this experiment's; a refusal of a log whose last frame is complete in length and damaged inside (a zeroed sector) is allowed and counted in refusals_corrupt_tail: the product fails closed and needs an operator; that is an availability limit and not a safety defect; synthetic seeded histories of 6 to 14 events; one process for the in-process arms, one machine profile; compaction, snapshots and retention are not crashed here.\n"
}
